The legal text is the Criminal Act 1991 of the Republic of the Sudan, as printed in the 9th Revised Edition of the
Laws of Sudan (قوانين السودان) by the Ministry of Justice, https://www.moj.gov.sd/sudanlaws/, retrieved 28 October 2026.
The edition carries the rights line "وزارة العدل - جمهورية السودان" and states no open licence.

Laws are not protected by copyright in Sudan. The Copyright and Neighbouring Rights Protection and Literal and
Artistic Works Act, 2013, section 6 reads: "The protection prescribed under the provisions of this Act shall not
include: ... (b) official document". Section 2 defines "Official documents" as "the official documents issued by the
State or its institutions, corporations or subsidiary units, including laws, Presidential and administrative orders,
International agreements and Judicial Judgments, arbitration awards and resolutions of the administrative committees
of Judicial Jurisdiction" (English text as published on WIPO Lex).

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per section; each section's marginal note was
moved into its heading line; footnote markers were dropped; spacing was normalised. The wording of the law was not
changed. The Government of Sudan does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages and the tools) are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
